# Beyond the Stars - CIRCUITS v2 clip (docs/recording.md; designs/docs/circuits-v2.md). About 100 s at 1920x1080, 30 fps.
# Sidereal (UMV), Empyrean (UXV) and Omega (MAX): wafers printed on star matter, Stellar SMDs, one Mainframe of each
# family out of a stock Assembly Line, ours in a stock recipe's any-of-tier slot, the raised Piko, a NAC run, the cost.
#
# Honesty rules (as showcase2.shots):
# - Everything is raised by script in a fresh creative superflat world, and the captions say so: the circuit chain
#   bench (/btsrecipes chain, B-136) builds stock GT machines on creative power and loads each machine in turn with
#   what the previous one made; stock parts and Eye fluids are supplied by script. The NAC bench (/btsrecipes nac,
#   B-133) builds a Nanochip Assembly Complex and loads one run. The machines do their own processing.
# - Long stretches run under the time warp (/btswarp, a cheat: the whole server runs N ticks per real tick through the
#   normal code); its tag shows the measured multiplier. A time-lapse tag shows frame sampling.
#
# Sites: the chain rig at (1000, 4, 1000) facing north (EBF 1000, Hyper-Intensity Laser Engraver 1008, Cutting
# Machine 1014, Assembling Machine 1016, Circuit Assembler 1018, chest 1020; the Assembly Line's controller at
# (1030, 6, 1014), its slices running west to x 1015); the NAC complex at (1300, 60, 1300), its Assembly Matrix at
# (1308, 54, 1275).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- setup (never recorded)
time day
command /gt cleanroom_bypass on cleanroom
command /btsrecipes chain build 1000 4 1000
name ebf 1000,4,1000
name hile 1008,4,1000
name cutter 1014,4,1000
name asm 1016,4,1000
name ca 1018,4,1000
name chest 1020,4,1000
name al 1030,6,1014
name alout 1015,4,1014
command /btsrecipes nac build 1300 60 1300
name nac 1300,60,1300
name matrix 1308,54,1275

# ================================================================ title
scene title
  card 4 Circuits v2 | Sidereal, Empyrean and Omega: three circuit families for UMV, UXV and MAX | printed on star matter from the Eye of Harmony

# ================================================================ the rig
scene rig
  caption Our circuits are made in stock GregTech machines. Here they stand side by side, built by script on creative power.
  label ebf side up | Electric Blast Furnace
  label hile side up | Laser Engraver (Hyper-Intensity)
  label ca side right | Cutting Machine, Assembling Machine, Circuit Assembler (UMV)
  label al side up | Assembly Line
  label chest side down | chest for the finished Mainframes
  dolly 1031,9,989 1023,9,988 seconds 7 look 1013,4,1007

# ================================================================ the steps, in NEI
scene nei-boule
  caption Step 1: a Stellar Boule, grown in the Blast Furnace from Raw Star Matter, the Eye of Harmony's first product.
  nei recipe sl.stellarBoule tab blast
  hold 3.5
  close

scene nei-wafer
  caption The boule is cut into Stellar Wafers; each family prints its own wafer with the matter of its Eye tier (Sidereal: Raw Star Matter).
  nei recipe sl.siderealWafer
  hold 3
  close

scene nei-ewafer
  caption Empyrean (UXV) wafers take White Dwarf Matter (Eye tier 4) with Excited Stellar Plasma Mixture...
  nei recipe sl.empyreanWafer
  hold 3
  close

scene nei-owafer
  caption ...and Omega (MAX) wafers take Black Dwarf Matter (Eye tier 5) with Hyperdense Stellar Mixture.
  nei recipe sl.omegaWafer
  hold 3
  close

scene nei-smd
  caption A new tier of SMD parts: Stellar SMDs, made from a Stellar Wafer and Excited Stellar Plasma Mixture (Eye tier 2 or the Homogeny).
  nei recipe sl.stellarSmdTransistor tab assembler
  hold 3
  close

# ================================================================ the chain, run for real
scene make-sid
  caption The whole chain runs here in those machines: each one loaded by script with what the last one made (stock parts supplied).
  goto 1028,9,989 look 1013,4,1007
  command /btsrecipes chain make sidereal 1000 4 1000
  warp 20
  timelapse 14 speed 1 until chainstep:SL-X24 tail 0
  warp off
  caption The Sidereal Mainframe (UMV) is assembled in the Assembly Line...
  goto 1030.5,7,1009.5 look 1030.5,6.5,1014.5
  gui al
  warp 6
  timelapse 8 speed 1 until chainidle tail 0.5
  close
  caption ...and goes into the chest. One Mainframe: 21 machine runs, about 660 billion EU.
  goto 1020.5,5.8,997.4 look 1020.5,4.5,1000.5
  use chest side north
  hold 2.5
  close

scene make-emp
  caption Empyrean (UXV): its Mainframe takes a Sidereal Mainframe and an Empyrean wafer printed on White Dwarf Matter.
  goto 1028,9,989 look 1013,4,1007
  command /btsrecipes chain make empyrean 1000 4 1000
  warp 20
  timelapse 9 speed 6 until chainstep:SL-X28 tail 0
  warp off
  goto 1030.5,7,1009.5 look 1030.5,6.5,1014.5
  gui al
  warp 7
  timelapse 8 speed 1 until chainidle tail 0.5
  close
  goto 1020.5,5.8,997.4 look 1020.5,4.5,1000.5
  use chest side north
  hold 2
  close

scene make-omega
  caption Omega (MAX): an Empyrean Mainframe inside, an Omega wafer printed on Black Dwarf Matter. No Eye tier 10 matter at all.
  goto 1028,9,989 look 1013,4,1007
  command /btsrecipes chain make omega 1000 4 1000
  warp 20
  timelapse 10 speed 14 until chainstep:SL-X32 tail 0
  warp off
  goto 1030.5,7,1009.5 look 1030.5,6.5,1014.5
  gui al
  warp 14
  timelapse 8 speed 1 until chainidle tail 0.5
  close
  caption One Mainframe of each family: Sidereal, Empyrean, Omega.
  goto 1020.5,5.8,997.4 look 1020.5,4.5,1000.5
  use chest side north
  hold 3
  close

# ================================================================ any circuit of the tier
scene any-umv
  caption Every recipe that asks for "any UMV circuit" takes ours: a stock GT recipe, the Mega Ultimate Buck Converter, made with two Sidereal Mainframes.
  goto 1016.5,5.6,997.4 look 1016.5,4.5,1000.5
  command /btsrecipes chain gt umv 1000 4 1000
  gui asm
  warp 2
  hold 5
  close

scene nei-any
  caption In NEI the same stock recipe, with our Mainframe in its "any UMV circuit" slot (top right, x2).
  nei usage sl.siderealMainframe tab assembler page 1
  hold 3.5
  close

scene nei-piko
  caption The pack's own UMV circuit, the Piko, now costs 2.5x the time and 2x the parts (Quantum and Planck too; a config option, on by default).
  nei recipe cc.PicoCircuit tab matrix
  hold 4
  close

# ================================================================ the NAC
scene nac
  caption Our circuits also run in GT's Nanochip Assembly Complex (built by script). Its Assembly Matrix, loaded by script with our parts...
  label matrix side up | Assembly Matrix
  goto 1308.5,57,1268 look 1308.5,55,1275.5
  hold 2.5
  label clear
  caption ...makes a Sidereal Mainframe (the NAC's own overclocks make it quick).
  goto 1308.5,55.6,1271.4 look 1308.5,54.5,1275.5
  gui matrix
  command /btsrecipes nac run SL-N15 1300 60 1300
  hold 4
  close
  command /btsrecipes nac status 1300 60 1300

scene nei-nac
  caption The Sidereal Mainframe's page in the Nanochip Assembly Matrix.
  nei recipe sl.siderealMainframe tab matrix
  hold 3
  close

# ================================================================ the cost
scene cost
  card 10 What one top circuit costs, in EU | UMV:  Sidereal Mainframe 0.66 trillion   vs   Piko 9.1 trillion today, 22 trillion raised | UXV:  Empyrean Mainframe 2.5 trillion   vs   Quantum 35 trillion today, 85 trillion raised | MAX:  Omega Mainframe 7.1 trillion   vs   Planck 100 trillion today, 250 trillion raised | Ours: about 14x cheaper than today's circuits, about 34x cheaper than the raised ones
